{"name":"Twilight Express","hex":"#1c3378","fetched":"2026-10-13","looked":{"definitions":[{"term":"twilight","whole":false,"parts":[{"part":"Noun","definitions":["The soft light in the sky seen before the rising and (especially) after the setting of the sun, occasioned by the illumination of the earth’s atmosphere by the direct rays of the sun and their reflection on the earth.","The time when said light is visible; the period between daylight and darkness."]},{"part":"Adjective","definitions":["Pertaining to or resembling twilight; faintly illuminated; obscure.","Synonym of mesopelagic (“Describing the pelagic zone of the ocean between the photic epipelagic and the aphotic bathypelagic zones, characterized by very minimal light.”)"]}],"link":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/twilight"},{"term":"express","whole":false,"parts":[{"part":"Adjective","definitions":["Moving or operating quickly, as a train not making local stops.","Specific or precise; directly and distinctly stated; not merely implied."]},{"part":"Noun","definitions":["A mode of transportation, often a train, that travels quickly or directly, either on a regular schedule or as a special or excursion. Express trains often pass through stations along the way without stopping at them.","a public utility vehicle, typically a jeepney, that traverses through an expressway"]}],"link":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/express"}],"entries":[{"title":"Twilight Express","blocks":[{"text":"The Twilight Express  was a limited express sleeping car train service operated by West Japan Railway Company in Japan from 1989 until March 2015. It ran between the city of Sapporo on the northern island of Hokkaido and Osaka in south-western Honshu, a distance of approximately 1,500 km (930 mi), with the journey taking between 22 and 23 hours. From May 2015 until March 2016, the train operated as a luxury cruise train between Osaka and Shimonoseki in western Japan."}],"image":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/8/82/Twilight_Express_EF81_44_20130106.jpg/330px-Twilight_Express_EF81_44_20130106.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Twilight_Express"},{"title":"Twilight","blocks":[{"text":"Twilight is daylight illumination produced by diffuse sky radiation when the Sun is below the horizon as sunlight from the upper atmosphere is scattered in a way that illuminates both the Earth's lower atmosphere and also the Earth's surface. Twilight also may be any period when this illumination occurs, including dawn and dusk."}],"image":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/d/d1/Twilight_description_full_day.svg/330px-Twilight_description_full_day.svg.png?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Twilight"}],"images":[{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/d/d9/Twilight_Express_EF81_43_20090831.jpg/120px-Twilight_Express_EF81_43_20090831.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 1x, https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/d/d9/Twilight_Express_EF81_43_20090831.jpg/250px-Twilight_Express_EF81_43_20090831.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 2x","src":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/d/d9/Twilight_Express_EF81_43_20090831.jpg/120px-Twilight_Express_EF81_43_20090831.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail","alt":"","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/File%3ATwilight_Express_EF81_43_20090831.jpg"},{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/a/a7/ED79_14_Twilight_Express_20130708.jpg/120px-ED79_14_Twilight_Express_20130708.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 1x, https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/a/a7/ED79_14_Twilight_Express_20130708.jpg/250px-ED79_14_Twilight_Express_20130708.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_ca